69
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,760
These yellowish glands on the vein of the pepper

70
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,660
contain the capsaicin.

71
00:03:56,760 --> 00:04:00,060
When those glands are broken, the capsaicin is released.

72
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,860
It comes into contact with your skin,

73
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,160
and that's why you feel the heat.

74
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,980
Capsaicin produces a sensation of heat,

75
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:14,240
just like fire in tissue receptors in the mouth, tongue,

76
00:04:14,241 --> 00:04:17,940
tongue, and lips.

77
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,780
Capsaicin binds to the receptors and sends a signal

78
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:23,280
to the brain that tricks it into thinking it's actually

79
