00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:57,020
Whew.

424
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,920
People generally like the hot burn

425
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:01,420
because it represents a constrained risk.

426
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:03,640
So it's much like riding a roller coaster,

427
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:05,640
the thrill you get of defying death,

428
00:23:05,740 --> 00:23:08,040
and you know you're not going to die.

429
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:13,180
But many just want the fire out, fast, friggin' hot.

430
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:15,640
But water won't stop the burn.

431
00:23:15,641 --> 00:23:18,040
It actually spreads the capsaicin oil around.

432
00:23:18,140 --> 00:23:19,380
Wow.

433
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,180
It's worse than it was before.

434
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:24,380
I'm not sure the water's helping, but.

435
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:26,480
Dairy products such as milk or ice cream

436
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:28,980
work much better.

437
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:30,680
Oh, this helps.

438
00:23:30,780 --> 00:23:31,680
This helps a lot.

439
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:32,800
This helps.

440
00:23:32,900 --> 00:23:34,600
Milk contains a protein called casein,

441
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:39,300
and casein binds or latches onto the capsaicin

442
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:42,200
and washes it away much like a detergent.

443
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:48,140
Even after the mouth burn goes away,

444
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:50,780
capsaicin isn't finished with you.

445
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:54,380
Last time I'll eat one of those.

446
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:56,980
Once we ingest hot and spicy food,

447
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:59,480
our stomachs secrete an excess of hydrochloric acid

448
00:23:59,580 --> 00:24:00,780
to digest it.

449
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:06,700
Normally, a sphincter muscle keeps the acid from flowing upward.

450
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:10,500
But for some of us, the muscle doesn't close tight enough,

451
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:13,300
and the hydrochloric acid overflows into the esophagus.

452
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:18,340
This condition is commonly known as heartburn.

453
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:25,620
Commercial antacid products made of chemical-based materials,

454
00:24:25,621 --> 00:24:29,660
generally calcium hydroxide, neutralizes the stomach acid.

455
00:24:34,220 --> 00:24:37,920
But what if you could stop the burn before it starts?

456
00:24:37,921 --> 00:24:39,840
A new generation of pain relief products

457
00:24:39,841 --> 00:24:42,000
may have the answer.

458
00:24:42,001 --> 00:24:45,640
They're called H2 blockers.

459
00:24:45,641 --> 00:24:51,420
H2 stands for histamine 2, a common chemical in the body.

460
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:56,760
Its role is to signal cells in the stomach to release acid.

461
00:24:56,860 --> 00:25:00,260
These newer medicines set up a sort of chemical roadblock,

462
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:03,260
interrupting the signals, reducing the amount of

463
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:04,760
hydrochloric acid in the stomach.

464
00:25:07,620 --> 00:25:10,260
So that way, you would take this before you eat,

465
00:25:10,360 --> 00:25:13,400
and then while you are eating, you will not have these cells

466
00:25:13,401 --> 00:25:16,400
actually secreting acid.

467
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:19,400
But chilies aren't the only burn around.

468
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:21,400
Horseradish...

469
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:24,400
Mustard...

470
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:26,400
Oh, man.

471
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,400
...and wasabi...

472
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:30,400
Oh, oh.

473
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:31,400
Ah!

474
00:25:31,500 --> 00:25:32,400
Oh!

475
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:36,400
Have perfected a whole new way to make you sweat.

476
00:25:36,500 --> 00:25:37,400
Ah!

477
00:25:37,401 --> 00:25:42,400
They might appear to be less than appetizing,

478
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:46,400
but these coarse, thick roots are the source of one of our

479
00:25:46,500 --> 00:25:49,340
favorite hot and spicy condiments.

480
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:52,340
Horseradish.

481
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:56,260
Each year, United States manufacturers produce 6 million

482
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:57,960
gallons of the creamy sauce.

483
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:02,960
The Morehouse food processing plant in the city of industry,

484
00:26:03,060 --> 00:26:07,400
California, makes 20 different horseradish brands.

485
00:26:07,401 --> 00:26:10,900
They roll out 5,000 jars daily.

486
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:14,040
Easily the hottest brand, Atomic horseradish,

487
00:26:14,140 --> 00:26:17,040
is made for a number of distributors,

488
00:26:17,140 --> 00:26:19,740
including true natural taste.

489
00:26:19,840 --> 00:26:25,060
This is Atomic horseradish, and it is aptly named.

490
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:32,060
It has extraordinary heat, but a tremendous amount of flavor.

491
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:34,460
Unlike chili peppers, there isn't a scale

492
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:36,760
to measure horseradish heat.

493
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:39,160
You've got to taste it.

494
00:26:39,260 --> 00:26:47,600
Oh, oh, oh, ah, oh, ah, ah, ah.

495
00:26:47,700 --> 00:26:49,000
Easy for you to say.

496
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:54,120
But horseradish heat comes from a volatile oil

497
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:59,220
enzyme called isothiocyanate, located in the plant's root.

498
00:27:02,620 --> 00:27:05,460
Unlike capsaicin, which affects the lips and tongue,

499
00:27:05,461 --> 00:27:06,720
tongue.

500
00:27:06,820 --> 00:27:10,100
The volatile horseradish oil dissipates quickly in the mouth

501
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:12,100
and floats up to the sinuses as a vapor.

502
00:27:15,040 --> 00:27:18,000
That's why your nose and eyes burn.

503
00:27:18,100 --> 00:27:21,780
My face feels very flushed, very warm, very pleasant.

504
00:27:21,880 --> 00:27:24,180
My sinuses are totally clear.

505
00:27:27,040 --> 00:27:29,280
The horseradish plant is native to Eastern Europe

506
00:27:29,380 --> 00:27:31,460
and Western Asia.

507
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:34,420
But today, up to 85% of the world's supply

508
00:27:34,421 --> 00:27:36,860
from Illinois.

509
00:27:36,960 --> 00:27:39,860
The name horseradish comes from the word horse,

510
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:43,000
an Old English term meaning rough for coarse,

511
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:46,800
and refers to the plant's root.

512
00:27:46,900 --> 00:27:49,140
These are horseradish roots.

513
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:52,400
They're bland, have no flavor, taste at all.

514
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:54,440
I can actually take a bite out of one.

515
00:27:58,040 --> 00:27:58,940
There's no heat.

516
00:28:01,520 --> 00:28:03,380
The trick to bringing on the heat

517
00:28:03,381 --> 00:28:07,280
or crush the root, releasing the volatile oil enzymes.

518
00:28:09,420 --> 00:28:11,920
The process begins as workers feed the roots

519
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:13,120
into a crushing machine.

520
00:28:16,220 --> 00:28:19,120
The pulp is sent to a 100-gallon holding tank.

521
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:25,440
As with Tabasco sauce, vinegar is added.

522
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:28,740
But in the case of horseradish, acetic acid in vinegar

523
00:28:28,840 --> 00:28:31,940
reacts with the volatile oil enzymes and arrests

524
00:28:31,941 --> 00:28:33,640
or stops the heat level.

525
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:40,080
The result is a creamy mixture, bottled and sealed immediately

